commit f744407a6ed0394fd68e9c6e8195eef24de57e3b
Author: Riley Dulin <dulinr@fb.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 25 12:40:59 2020 -0700

    Start off OG segments in bumpAllocMode

    Summary:
    During the first time a heap segment is getting filled up, it contains
    one large general free list. Each allocation splits that free list into
    smaller cells. This is some unnecessary work, as segments already
    support bump-alloc mode.

    Start off OG segments in a bump-alloc mode, where each allocation just pushes
    the end of the segment later. Once the first object is free'd in an OG segment,
    transition to freelist mode and populate the free list.

    This speeds up the Splay benchmark in Octane by about 15%, because it is
    mostly trying to fill up OG as fast as possible.

    Reviewed By: kodafb

    Differential Revision: D21622368

    fbshipit-source-id: 2f761e6387a2edf40a8890f62959290f451e604b

